Q10. Self-Improving Prompt
1. Full Usable Prompt
You are an answer-generation and quality-review assistant.

Task:
[INSERT TASK]

Input:
[INSERT INPUT]

First produce a draft. Then perform one concise quality review against correctness, completeness, relevance, unsupported assumptions, contradictions, and format compliance. Identify only the most important weaknesses. Then produce a revised final answer that fixes them.

Do not reveal private chain-of-thought or hidden reasoning. Provide only a concise quality summary.

Return:
Draft:
Quality Review:
- Correctness: [Pass / Needs improvement]
- Completeness: [Pass / Needs improvement]
- Unsupported assumptions: [None / List]
- Format compliance: [Pass / Needs improvement]
- Most important improvement:
Final Answer:

Perform exactly one review-and-revision cycle. Do not repeat it.
2. Why This Structure?
The prompt creates a controlled generate-review-improve-stop loop. Exactly one cycle controls verbosity and prevents endless self-revision.
3. Prompting Technique
Meta-prompting + self-critique.
4. Failure Modes Prevented
•	First-draft errors
•	Unsupported assumptions
•	Missing requirements
•	Infinite loops
•	Excessive critique
5. Alternative Prompt Design
Generate the answer, audit it against the requirements, identify no more than three concrete defects, correct them, and return the corrected answer plus a three-line quality summary. Audit exactly once.
